content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22120, filtered-water line; line is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Dry running: the applicable requirement is Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and 'never run dry'; no permissible dry-run duration is given. The reported approximately 15 minutes dry therefore exceeded the operating limit. The pump is now primed, but that does not establish that the seal is undamaged.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 classifier, using velocity in mm/s RMS on the bearing housings and classifying the highest reading from both housings. Treating the reported 3.0 mm/s as being on that measurement basis, it falls in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is above the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary, below the 4.5 Zone C 'Restricted - plan maintenance' threshold, and below the 7.1 Zone D threshold. It therefore does not activate the site rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: the applicable bearing-housing limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 69 C is within the normal range, 1 C below its upper value, and below both alarm and trip. It does not trigger the site requirement for a priority-1 work order, which applies above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no shaft-seal leakage has been seen yet. Dry running is a documented probable cause of leakage through worn or cracked seal faces, so absence of leakage at this early check does not confirm internal seal condition. No numerical leakage limit is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Loss of prime or effective discharge-fed Plan 11 seal flush during the tank changeover, resulting in the confirmed dry-running event. The precise reason flush/prime was lost is not established by the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible mechanical-seal face wear or cracking caused by running dry, with delayed shaft-seal leakage as the principal concern. This remains unconfirmed because no leakage has yet been observed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before the scheduled isolation, inspect again for shaft-seal leakage and record the housing temperature. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Maintain prime and Plan 11 flush while the pump remains in service; record all as-found readings on the work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the seal work, isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent the line, and obtain a line-break permit before opening the pump. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because this filtered-water line is dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before removing the back pull-out assembly, arrange a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the site's 25 kg threshold for these controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller. Withdraw the existing seal and sleeve; inspect and record the seal-face condition and sleeve scoring. Do not replace bearings solely on the current 3.0 mm/s and 69 C readings. If either bearing is found to have wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the planned precautionary post-dry-run seal replacement, fit one new HF3-450B cartridge seal; do not fit HF3-450. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Separately assess the existing sleeve for scoring and replace it with HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using the applicable torques. Table 5 values, for lightly oiled threads, are: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm and, if disturbed, M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. For the HF3-450B seal gland nuts, use the service-bulletin torque of 30 Nm, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment when correcting shaft-seal leakage, and use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Record the result against parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular alignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, refit and secure the assembly, vent and prime the casing, and confirm Plan 11 flush from pump discharge is available; never run the pump dry. After restart, inspect for seal leakage and repeat both-housing vibration and housing-temperature checks. If vibration enters Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift; the documented trip limit is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; one required for the planned replacement and mandatory in place of HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new whenever the casing is opened for the seal work.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; stage one as a contingency and install only if existing sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Any work inside the pump or on its seal requires electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves because P-101 is on a filtered-water line dosed with sodium hypochlorite.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly requires lifting equipment and, because it exceeds 25 kg, a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment standard allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours. Include this when alignment is required because the motor or bearing housing was moved, or when the leak-related alignment check is performed.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement allowance, not included in the planned seal-work total: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12.0 technician-hours, only if the documented wear, noise or high-temperature criteria are found.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies specifically to HF-300 pumps with serial HF3-22000 and above. P-101's serial HF3-22120 is within that range. Therefore, do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. The manual-based continuation for pumps below HF3-22000 does not apply to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque: manual section 5.2 refers tightening to Table 5, which lists 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. The serial-applicable SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Use 30 Nm on P-101; the 25 Nm value is not applicable to this replacement. The other Table 5 fastener torques remain applicable where their fasteners are disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 3.0 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what were the separate drive-end and non-drive-end readings? The Zone B assessment is provisional until the Figure 3 measurement basis and highest reading are confirmed (C06, C07).",
    "What caused the loss of prime or Plan 11 flush during tank changeover, and what change to the changeover method will prevent recurrence? The evidence gives the flush arrangement and dry-run prohibition but no event root cause or specific changeover controls (C02).",
    "Has any leakage developed since the initial report, and what are the as-found seal-face and sleeve-scoring conditions? The external readings cannot confirm or exclude internal dry-run damage (C02, C09, C10, C13).",
    "The manual directs seal replacement for leakage associated with worn or cracked faces or dry running, but it does not state that every dry run automatically requires replacement. Confirm whether the planner's precautionary replacement scope is to proceed as planned or be changed to inspection-only after internal examination (C02, C09, C10).",
    "No site response-time matrix for P2 versus P3 is supplied; only the P1 trigger above the bearing-temperature alarm limit is documented. Confirm the required completion date for this P2 dry-run follow-up (C02, C15)."
  ]
}
